name: "FauciPaulHearingFull"

# ============================================================================
# THE FAUCI / PAUL DISPUTE -- as it actually stands.
#
# EVERY CLAIM IN THIS FILE CORRESPONDS TO SOMETHING THAT HAPPENED OR A
# POSITION SOMEONE ACTUALLY TOOK. Nothing is invented. In particular there
# are NO CONCEDE_CHALLENGE steps, because neither party has conceded
# anything. The dispute is unresolved, and the scenario ends unresolved.
#
# That makes this a CONSTRUCTION test, not a propagation test. It exercises
# multi-from relations, definitions inside from-sets, independent supports,
# and challenge attachment. Concede propagation is covered by
# ConcedePropagationTest.pbtxt -- do not add concessions here to get more
# coverage, because any concession in this file would be fiction.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TIMELINE OF RECORD
#
#   2014        NIAID awards a grant to EcoHealth Alliance, later renewed in
#               2019, including a sub-award to the Wuhan Institute of
#               Virology. Cancelled April 2020, later reinstated with
#               conditions EcoHealth said it could not meet.
#   2014-2017   Federal funding pause on certain gain-of-function work.
#   2017        The pause is replaced with a review framework for "enhanced
#               potential pandemic pathogens" (EPPP) -- pathogens already
#               highly transmissible and virulent in humans that have been
#               made more so.
#   May 2021    Fauci tells a Senate hearing: "The NIH has not ever and does
#               not now fund gain-of-function research in the Wuhan Institute
#               of Virology."
#   Jul 2021    Paul accuses Fauci of lying to Congress, citing the criminal
#               statute. Fauci calls the accusation false.
#   Oct 2021    NIH Principal Deputy Director Lawrence Tabak writes to Rep.
#               Comer describing a "limited experiment" in which mice
#               infected with a chimeric SHC014-WIV1 bat coronavirus became
#               sicker than those infected with WIV1, and stating EcoHealth
#               failed to report that result promptly as the grant required.
#               The letter also says the result was unexpected rather than an
#               objective, and that the viruses could not have produced
#               SARS-CoV-2. Both sides read this letter as vindicating them.
#   Jun 2026    Paul subpoenas Fauci after Fauci withdraws from voluntary
#               testimony.
#   Jul 25-27   Paul releases 1,100+ pages of Fauci's journals covering
#               December 2019 to December 2022. HHS Secretary Kennedy says
#               the records were recovered from 11 government servers over
#               eight months. Fauci was not notified before publication.
#   Jul 29 2026 Fauci invokes the Fifth Amendment and declines to answer,
#               reportedly 111 times.
#   Aug 6 2026  The committee votes 8-5 to hold Fauci in contempt, along
#               party lines. Paul sends the referral directly to the Justice
#               Department, bypassing a Senate floor vote.
#
#   CURRENT STATUS: unresolved. No party has withdrawn any position. A legal
#   fight over the scope of the Fifth Amendment claim appears likely.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THE ENGINE CANNOT EXPRESS (see section 6 of the scenario guide)
#
#   [SUB-A] OPPOSE targeting a RELATION. Several counters below dispute an
#      INFERENCE while accepting the evidence -- Fauci does not deny the
#      journals are his, and does not deny the Tabak letter says what it
#      says. Those are attacks on the link and should yield UNSUPPORTED with
#      the evidence untouched. Only claims can be targeted, so each is
#      rendered as a claim-level challenge -- stronger than the case warrants.
#
#   [GAP-B] CONTESTED. Nothing here is resolved, and several branches have
#      real surviving support on both sides. Three statuses cannot say so.
#
#   [GAP-C] ACCEPTED. Claims 3, 4, 10 and 11 are not disputed by either
#      party. There is no way to mark common ground, so they look identical
#      to claims nobody has examined.
#
#   [GAP-D] The definitional lens. The verdict on claim 2 should flip with
#      the reader's choice between claim 5 and claim 6, writing nothing.
#
#   [GAP-E] The author lane. The provenance of the journals is disputed and
#      should be debatable without threatening what they say.
#
#   [GAP-F] The origin question (lab incident vs natural spillover) is
#      OMITTED. It is CONTESTED in its purest form and is not a sub-claim of
#      anything here. It needs its own scenario.
#
#   [GAP-G] There is no way to express that Fauci declined to engage -- which
#      is what the 2026 hearing WAS. See BRANCH D.
#
# 22 claims. Ids noted beside every action.
# ============================================================================

steps { action { username: "paul"  event_type: "CREATE_USER" } }
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "CREATE_USER" } }

# claim 1 -- the root. Paul's overall position.
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "CREATE_DEBATE"
    debate_topic: "Fauci was dishonest with Congress and the public about COVID-19"
  }
}

steps { action { username: "paul"  event_type: "JOIN_DEBATE"  debate_id: 1 } }
steps { action { username: "paul"  event_type: "ENTER_DEBATE" debate_id: 1 } }
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "JOIN_DEBATE"  debate_id: 1 } }
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "ENTER_DEBATE" debate_id: 1 } }

steps {
  expectations { check_type: "CLAIM_EXISTS" claim_id: 1 }
  expectations { check_type: "COLLECTION_SIZE" expected_count: 1 }
  expectations { check_type: "ENGAGEMENT_STATE" username: "paul"  expected_action: "ACTION_DEBATING" }
  expectations { check_type: "ENGAGEMENT_STATE" username: "fauci" expected_action: "ACTION_DEBATING" }
}

# ============================================================================
# BRANCH A -- the perjury charge and the definition it turns on
# ============================================================================

# claim 2 -- first of three independent supports for the root
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 1 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "Fauci's May 2021 testimony that NIH did not fund gain-of-function research at the Wuhan Institute was false"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

# claims 3, 4, 5 -- ONE relation, THREE from-claims, the third a DEFINITION.
#
# THE CENTRAL MECHANISM.
#
# Claims 3 and 4 are NOT IN DISPUTE. Fauci has never denied the grant existed
# or denied saying what he said. They establish claim 2 only under a
# particular reading of the term, supplied by claim 5. Change claim 5 and the
# same undisputed facts stop supporting the accusation.
#
# Claim 5 is the definition NIH itself published on its website before
# October 2021, which is why Paul can present it as the standard meaning
# rather than one he invented.
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 2 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "NIAID awarded a grant to EcoHealth Alliance, renewed in 2019, that included a sub-award to the Wuhan Institute of Virology"
    extra_claim_texts: "In May 2021 Senate testimony Fauci said the NIH has not ever and does not now fund gain-of-function research in the Wuhan Institute of Virology"
    extra_claim_texts: "Gain-of-function research means research that modifies a biological agent so that it confers new or enhanced activity to that agent"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

steps {
  expectations { check_type: "COLLECTION_SIZE" expected_count: 5 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_COUNT" to_claim_id: 2 expected_count: 3 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 3 to_claim_id: 2 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 4 to_claim_id: 2 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 5 to_claim_id: 2 }
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 3 username: "paul" expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 4 username: "paul" expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
}

# claim 6 -- [SUB-A] Fauci challenges the DEFINITION, not the facts.
# His stated position throughout has been that the term has a specific
# regulatory meaning and the funded work fell outside it.
#
# Marked DEFINITIONAL, which is exactly what it is: Fauci disputes no fact
# here, only what the term covers. Without the basis the engine would store
# this identically to an evidential challenge.
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 5 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "fauci"
    event_type: "SUBMIT_CHALLENGE_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "The standard governing federal funding decisions is enhanced potential pandemic pathogen, meaning a pathogen already highly transmissible and virulent in humans that has been made more so"
    challenge_description: "The applicable definition is the regulatory one, not a general one."
    basis: "DEFINITIONAL"
  }
}

# claims 7, 8 -- AUTHORITY-basis support for the regulatory definition
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 6 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "fauci"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "In 2017 federal officials replaced the 2014 to 2017 funding pause with a review framework for enhanced potential pandemic pathogens"
    extra_claim_texts: "NIH stated in 2021 that the Wuhan studies did not require that additional review because they involved bat coronaviruses genetically distant from the pandemic virus"
    basis: "AUTHORITY"
  }
}

steps {
  expectations { check_type: "COLLECTION_SIZE" expected_count: 8 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_COUNT" to_claim_id: 6 expected_count: 2 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 7 to_claim_id: 6 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 8 to_claim_id: 6 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_COUNT" link_type: "CHALLENGE" expected_count: 1 }
}

# ============================================================================
# BRANCH B -- the Tabak letter
#
# The single most contested document in the dispute, and the clearest case in
# the whole file of UNDISPUTED EVIDENCE WITH A DISPUTED INFERENCE. Nobody
# argues about what the letter says. Both sides cite it as vindication.
# ============================================================================

# claim 9 -- a SECOND, independent support for claim 2.
# Separate ADD_CHILD_CLAIM on the same parent = separate relation = OR.
# If the definitional branch fails, this one still stands on its own.
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 2 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "The October 2021 NIH letter confirms the funded work enhanced a virus"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

# claims 10, 11 -- ONE relation, TWO from-claims. Neither party disputes
# either of these. [GAP-C]
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 9 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "In an October 2021 letter to Rep. Comer, NIH official Lawrence Tabak described a limited experiment in which mice infected with a chimeric SHC014-WIV1 bat coronavirus became sicker than those infected with WIV1"
    extra_claim_texts: "The same letter states EcoHealth Alliance failed to report that result promptly as the grant terms required"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

# claim 12 -- [SUB-A] the counter-reading of the same letter.
# This disputes the INFERENCE, not the document. In the target design it
# attacks the relation [10,11] -> 9 and claim 9 becomes UNSUPPORTED while
# claims 10 and 11 stay standing.
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 9 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "fauci"
    event_type: "SUBMIT_CHALLENGE_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "The same letter states the result was unexpected rather than an objective of the research, and that the viruses studied could not have produced SARS-CoV-2"
    challenge_description: "The letter is not in dispute. What follows from it is."
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

steps {
  expectations { check_type: "COLLECTION_SIZE" expected_count: 12 }
  # claim 2 now has TWO independent supporting relations: [3,4,5] and [9]
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 9 to_claim_id: 2 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_COUNT" to_claim_id: 9 expected_count: 2 }
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 10 username: "paul" expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 11 username: "paul" expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
}

# ============================================================================
# BRANCH C -- the journals
# ============================================================================

# claim 13 -- second independent support for the root
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 1 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "Fauci's public statements about the virus's origin differed from his private view"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

# claims 14, 15 -- ONE relation, TWO from-claims, jointly required.
# The private record alone shows only uncertainty, which is not dishonesty.
# The public statement alone shows only a stated position. Only together do
# they support a divergence claim.
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 13 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "Fauci's journals covering December 2019 to December 2022 record uncertainty about the origin of the virus"
    extra_claim_texts: "Early in the pandemic Fauci publicly said the evidence pointed very, very strongly toward a natural origin"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

# claim 16 -- [SUB-A] the counter. Again an inference dispute: the journals'
# authenticity is not questioned by anyone.
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 13 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "fauci"
    event_type: "SUBMIT_CHALLENGE_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "Recording uncertainty privately while stating a leading hypothesis publicly is ordinary scientific caution rather than a contradiction"
    challenge_description: "The journals are genuine. The inference from them does not follow."
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

# ============================================================================
# BRANCH D -- the 2026 hearing and the Fifth Amendment
#
# [GAP-G] What actually happened is that Fauci declined to engage. In the
# target design that is ABANDONED -- silence recorded as silence, explicitly
# not concession and explicitly not defeat. There is no way to say it here,
# so the inference drawn FROM the silence is entered as an ordinary claim and
# the objection to that inference as an ordinary challenge. That makes a
# constitutional question look like a factual one.
# ============================================================================

# claim 17 -- third independent support for the root
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 1 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "Fauci's refusal to answer the committee's questions indicates he could not answer them truthfully"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

# claims 18, 19 -- ONE relation, TWO from-claims
steps { action { username: "paul" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 17 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "paul"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "At the July 29 2026 hearing Fauci invoked the Fifth Amendment and declined to answer the committee's questions"
    extra_claim_texts: "Senator Johnson said it would be almost impossible for Fauci to answer the questions truthfully without demonstrating what he did"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

# claim 20 -- the objection. A legal-principle claim: no evidence settles
# whether an inference from silence is legitimate, so this is normative
# rather than factual. The engine has no way to mark that on a challenge.
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 17 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "fauci"
    event_type: "SUBMIT_CHALLENGE_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "Invoking the Fifth Amendment is a constitutional right from which no inference of wrongdoing follows"
    challenge_description: "Silence under a right is not evidence."
    basis: "NORMATIVE"
  }
}

# claims 21, 22 -- ONE relation, TWO from-claims supporting the objection.
# These are the two reasons actually advanced: that answering carried real
# legal exposure, and that the exposure was the point.
steps { action { username: "fauci" event_type: "GO_TO_CLAIM" claim_id: 20 } }
steps {
  action {
    username: "fauci"
    event_type: "ADD_CHILD_CLAIM"
    claim_text: "The 2025 pardon covers conduct between 2014 and January 2025 and would not protect statements made in present-day testimony"
    extra_claim_texts: "Senator Hassan said the aim was to wait for a misstatement not covered by the pardon and then bring charges over it"
    basis: "EVIDENTIAL"
  }
}

# ---- full structure ------------------------------------------------------
steps {
  expectations { check_type: "COLLECTION_SIZE" expected_count: 22 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_COUNT" link_type: "PARENT_CHILD" expected_count: 10 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_COUNT" link_type: "CHALLENGE"    expected_count: 4 }

  # the root's three independent supports
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 2  to_claim_id: 1 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 13 to_claim_id: 1 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 17 to_claim_id: 1 }

  # every multi-from relation in the file
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_COUNT" to_claim_id: 2  expected_count: 3 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_COUNT" to_claim_id: 6  expected_count: 2 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_COUNT" to_claim_id: 9  expected_count: 2 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_COUNT" to_claim_id: 13 expected_count: 2 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_COUNT" to_claim_id: 17 expected_count: 2 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_COUNT" to_claim_id: 20 expected_count: 2 }

  # every challenge is attached to the claim it actually targets
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 6  to_claim_id: 5  }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 12 to_claim_id: 9  }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 16 to_claim_id: 13 }
  expectations { check_type: "RELATION_FROM_EXISTS" from_claim_id: 20 to_claim_id: 17 }

  # undisputed evidence stands
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 3  username: "paul"  expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 4  username: "paul"  expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 10 username: "paul"  expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 11 username: "paul"  expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 18 username: "paul"  expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
  expectations { check_type: "USER_VIEW" claim_id: 21 username: "fauci" expected_status: "TRUE_CLAIM" }
}

# ============================================================================
# THE SCENARIO ENDS HERE, UNRESOLVED -- because the dispute is unresolved.
#
# No CONCEDE_CHALLENGE step appears in this file. Neither party has withdrawn
# a position. Adding one to exercise propagation would be inventing an event,
# and a scenario built from a real dispute must not contain fabricated moves.
#
# WHAT A PASS MEANS
#   Six multi-from relations build correctly, including one holding a
#   definition alongside the facts it qualifies. Three independent relations
#   coexist on the root and two on claim 2. Four challenges attach to the
#   claims they actually target. Undisputed evidence stands.
#
# WHAT A PASS DOES NOT MEAN
#   The four counters in this file (claims 6, 12, 16, 20) all dispute an
#   INFERENCE while accepting the evidence -- that is the shape of this entire
#   dispute, and it is the one thing the engine cannot represent. Every one is
#   rendered as a claim-level challenge instead, which says something stronger
#   than any party actually said.
#
#   Nothing in the file distinguishes the four claims both parties agree on
#   from claims nobody has examined. Nothing expresses that the origin
#   question has real support on both sides. And nothing expresses that the
#   2026 hearing consisted of a witness declining to speak.
#
#   A green run certifies the plumbing. It does not certify that the tool can
#   hold this argument.
# ============================================================================
